title The card breathes and the sameness measured -- the air rota lap condenses the pin and counts the duplicate bodies
prompt Keaton granted the recommended doors by his word; mid-lap he asked whether sameness-is-the-macro condensing applies to our scripts with more Rishi conversions, especially the Pond family, toward retiring the ai-jail dependency.
think The air row read first, as declared: the threshold (touch works only at a surface, so a boundary is tested by pressing on it) and single-stranded (simple is a fact about the object, checked by pulling one part out; the easy path returns wearing the face of speed). TAME_CORE and GAUGE_STYLE are held from this session's constant use rather than reread whole, said honestly here. The condense then WAS the row's own exercise: a page one byte from its bound is a boundary the hand passed through.
think The mechanism of the condense: a checkpoint row seats in construction/CHECKPOINTS.md with walk-back nib e4e80e5677; a new archive file construction/archive/20260829-141640_itinerary-settled-decisions.md takes the Compass Chapter table, four granted Open-doors rows, the duplicate cadence section, and the two landed Now paragraphs word for word; construction/ITINERARY.md replaces them with pointer lines, seats the LOCA ladder's paragraph as the Now block, and moves the Prior-laps row forward. The card falls 24,575 to 22,762 bytes against its 24,576 bound.
think The sameness survey, measured with comm over sorted files: tools/equinox/almanac/ holds 114 almanac scripts of about 39 lines with 26 lines identical between two sampled members -- two thirds of each file is one shared body, the note_path shape at 114x. comlink/ holds 15 run_*_wire_lab.sh of about 12 lines sharing 8. The four launchers share ZERO literal lines -- their jail/pond duplication is a branch repeated in idea rather than bytes, which is why pond_seal_gate must find three admission sites by git grep: the sameness was never pulled into one door.
obs The Pond-serving move is therefore not a text macro: it is one enclosure door -- a single Rishi entry (an enclosure_enter shape) all launchers call, holding the seal check, the pond admission, and the jail fallback in one file, so the gate guards one site and the ai-jail retirement becomes a single deletion when Pond lands. The seal script tools/p/pond_exit_bron_master_seal.sh (92 lines, operational) molts .sh to .rish on that same touch under the seated rule. The almanac and wire-lab condenses are ratchet-shaped campaigns, not reds -- nothing is wrong, two families are not yet uniform -- and a 114-file sweep wants its own round with output-parity proven before any file leaves.
obs Cross-seat caution kept: the launchers are run by every body, so the one-door pull is recommended rather than executed; the peer's in-flight witness edits were never touched, and this lap's commit is pathspec-limited to its own five files.
